  "body": "Proposal only. **Do not merge without Kyle's approval** (pushing `main` deploys the site).\n\nThese edits fix the Raspberry Pi setup pages where they disagree with the lab's real robot Pis. Each commit names its row in `vehicles/HIPPOCAMPUS/pi/SETUP-PARITY.md` (underwater-localization repo) and its evidence: `hippo-main-02` (manifest captured 2026-08-17, the authority), `hippo-main-03` (live probe 2026-08-19), and the org apt repository (read live 2026-09-16). `hippo-main-01` was rebuilt to the same standard on 2026-09-16 (Ubuntu 24.04 arm64, all health checks passing before and after a reboot); two follow-up commits below use its fresh image as evidence.\n\n`python3 tools/check.py` is all green on the branch tip. The search shard was rebuilt with `tools/build_search_index.py --site-only`. No `tools/`, `.github/` or `api/` changes.\n\n## The 12 Phase 3 items\n\n| # | Item | Row | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | Plaintext password and personal key comments in the cloud-init example | R28 | **Already fixed on the site.** `raspberry-pi/ubuntu-24-04-server.md` has `# plain_text_passwd: \"<set-your-own-password>\"` and `- <your-ssh-public-key>`. |\n| 3.2 | Pinout page empty | R15 | **Already fixed on the site.** `raspberry-pi/pinout.md` line 9 shows the UUV pinout image (SDA4/SCL4 on GPIO6/7 marked \"ESCs\", TL2 on uart5). Only the BlueROV (buddy) tab is still a to-do. |\n| 3.3 | chrony and the first-boot clock | R29 | **Fixed** (15b36e9) |\n| 3.4 | unattended-upgrades dpkg lock | R31 | **Fixed** (04d689e) |\n| 3.5 | `ros2.list` -> `ros2-apt-source` | R03 | **Fixed** (46ab801) |\n| 3.6 | `uart3`; `i2c_arm` and `i2c6` | R10, R11 | **Fixed** (0d6ccd2, b658ad1). The Ubuntu page already had `uart3`; the UART page did not. |\n| 3.7 | `fcu_tele` -> `fcu_data`; mavlink-router `Device` | R14, R48 | **Fixed** (64a3a09, 4b5c6b6) |\n| 3.8 | Package list and architecture | R04, R05 | **Fixed** (be37c3c) |\n| 3.9 | Ethernet hook for ifupdown | R32 | **Fixed, marked untested** (c511621) |\n| 3.10 | wifi/BT overlays; iniVation and uhubctl udev rules; 24.04 iniVation route | R33, R35, R49 | **Fixed** R33 (c25803c) and R35 (e51210f). R49 **already covered**: `lab-cameras/event-cameras.md` builds libcaer from source via `libcaer_driver`'s `vcs import`. |\n| 3.11 | Pi clone list; `hippo_core/` script path | R19, R20 | **Half fixed.** R20 fixed (d9db0f7). R19 **not changed**: which packages a Pi workspace should hold is the lab's decision (SETUP-PARITY §E question 4). The lab Pi used personal `FinnBreu` forks for `hardware` and `hippo_guidance`, which should not go into org docs without that decision. New evidence (2026-09-16): `https://github.com/FinnBreu/hippo_guidance.git` now returns \"Repository not found\", so a clone list naming it would fail today. |\n| 3.12 | arm64 `acoustic-msgs` build | R06 | **Not a docs change.** Request text below; nothing was sent. |\n\nCount: 8 fixed on this branch (3.3-3.10), 1 half fixed (3.11), 2 already fixed on the site (3.1, 3.2), 1 not a docs change (3.12).\n\n## Follow-up commits from the `hippo-main-01` rebuild (2026-09-16)\n\n- `8f00595` (R29, R31; items 3.3, 3.4): listing `chrony` in cloud-init cannot prevent the first-boot clock failure, because `chrony` is one of the packages that fail; run `apt-get update` before re-running the installs (else `404 Not Found`); SSH is refused for a few minutes while apt upgrades `openssh-server`. All three seen on 01's first boot.\n- `783a191` (R10; item 3.6): the stock Ubuntu 24.04.4 `config.txt` already has `dtparam=i2c_arm=on` (and `enable_uart=1`) in the right place, so a fresh image needs only the two I2C `dtoverlay=` lines.\n\nThe item counts below are unchanged.\n\n## Request text for 3.12 (draft, not sent)\n\n> The org apt repository (Release dated 29 Aug 2025) publishes `ros-jazzy-acoustic-msgs` for amd64 but not for arm64, and there is no `binary-all` component. `ros-jazzy-hippo-robot` 1.0.3-0noble depends on it, so the documented Raspberry Pi install (`sudo apt install ros-jazzy-hippo-robot`) fails on every Pi with \"Depends: ros-jazzy-acoustic-msgs but it is not installable\". An arm64 build existed earlier (hippo-main-02 had `ros-jazzy-acoustic-msgs 0.0.1-0noble` arm64 installed). Could you publish the arm64 build again?\n\n## Noticed, not changed here\n\n- `raspberry-pi/uart-configuration.md` line 40: the UART/KERNELS/GPIO table is a flattened RST table and renders as one line of `====`.\n- `raspberry-pi/quality-of-life.md`: the zsh setup uses `echo '...\\n...'`, which writes literal `\\n` when run from bash (R34).\n- `concepts/ros2-workspace.md` still lists `hippo_core` in its example tree (tied to R19).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
